     "content": {
      "id": "v2-proposal-j3-022101-root",
      "type": "question",
      "label": null,
      "prompt": "Graph $y=\\sqrt{x}-\\dfrac{1}{x}$.",
      "questionDiagrams": [],
      "answer": {
       "short": "Domain $x>0$, with vertical asymptote $x=0$ ($y\\to-\\infty$) and $x$-intercept $(1,0)$. The graph increases throughout, rising without bound and staying below $y=\\sqrt{x}$.",
       "worked": "Sketch $y=\\sqrt{x}$ and $y=-\\frac1x$ (the reflection of $y=\\frac1x$ in the $x$-axis) lightly. The common domain is $x>0$. Add their ordinates.\n$$\\begin{align*}y\\left(\\tfrac14\\right)&=\\frac12-4=-\\frac72\\\\y\\left(\\tfrac12\\right)&=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}-2\\approx-1.3\\\\y(1)&=1-1=0\\\\y(4)&=2-\\frac14=\\frac74\\\\y(9)&=3-\\frac19=\\frac{26}{9}\\end{align*}$$\nFor the $x$-intercept:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x}&=\\frac1x\\\\x\\sqrt{x}&=1\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nNear $x=0$, $-\\frac1x\\to-\\infty$ dominates, so the graph falls without bound. For large $x$, $-\\frac1x\\to0$, so the graph follows $y=\\sqrt{x}$ from below. Both components increase, so the sum increases. Join the points smoothly.",
       "solutionDiagrams": [
        {
         "id": "v2-proposal-j3-022101-j3-solution",
         "format": "tikz",
         "widthMm": 61,
         "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"sumBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"result curve; dashed pale curves are the components\"}],\"reference\":\"j3 replacement solution\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.7cm,>=stealth,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{sumBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-0.5,-4.7) rectangle (9.6,3.7);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (-0.3,0)--(9.3,0) node[below] {$x$};\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (0,-4.4)--(0,3.4) node[above left] {$y$};\n\\draw[sumBlue,opacity=0.65,dashed,line width=0.8pt,->] plot[domain=0.02:9,samples=100] (\\x,{sqrt(\\x)});\n\\draw[sumBlue,opacity=0.65,dashed,line width=0.8pt,<->] plot[domain=0.25:9,samples=120] (\\x,{-1/\\x});\n\\draw[sumBlue,line width=0.8pt,<->] plot[domain=0.22:9,samples=200] (\\x,{sqrt(\\x)-1/\\x});\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (1,-0.1)--(1,0.1);\n\\node[black,anchor=north,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (1,-0.12) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$1$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\end{tikzpicture}"
        }
       ]
      }
